{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500737-chary-counselor-s-setting-artifact-\u25cf\u25cf","id":1500737,"title":"Chary Counselor's Setting (Artifact \u25cf\u25cf)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-19T09:51:49-08:00","id":1500737,"title":"Chary Counselor's Setting (Artifact \u25cf\u25cf)","content":"Huzzah! The forums live again! Figured I'd celebrate by bringing over a little artifact I made that I was rather pleased with. Though I'm lazy, so just copied the whole text...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While talking with some fellow fans about what ridiculous spoils my player's might find when raiding the V'neef compound on Wu-Jian. One of the ideas that was mentioned was &quot;solid moonsilver chopsticks. Not artifacts, just moonsilver chopsticks&quot;, which a definitely fun idea but it combined in my head with the interesting history of metal chopsticks and an excellent moment in the criminally underrated wuxia film The Butcher, The Chef, and The Swordsman. So here's the result.<br /> <br /> Chary Counselor's Setting (Artifact \u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Moonsilver table setting, Attunement 1m/1wp<br /> <br /> It is a long held belief across Creation that silver will tarnish the moment it comes into contact with poison, leading to it being the preffered material for dining utensils among those wealthy enough to afford it. An exceptionally wealthy, and exceptionally paranoid, official of the early Shogunate was the first to design and commission these utensils. The scarcity of the materials used in their creation has led to few seeking to duplicate the design, but as Dynasts prowl for more and more tools for the looming civil war the demand for them has started to grow. The setting is comprised of a spoon and a pair of chopsticks, both of which are carved from solid moonsilver and inlaid with intricate designs of unalloyed green jade. The exact designs of the inlay are up to the individual crafter but the materials are non-negotiable if they are to serve their intended purpose. While the simple opulence of the setting would likely be enough, their true purpose extends beyond simply a sign of wealth and power. The almost living nature of the moonsilver paired with the wood essence of the green jade make the items almost infallible at the detection of poisons. A being capable of manipulating Essence can attune to the items by comminting 1 mote, and an exceptionally determined and paranoid mortal can attune to the item by committing 1 willpower. While attuned the moonsilver blackens almost the instant it comes in contact poison, whether the spoon is dipped into a poisoned broth or the chopsticks are used to pick up a poisoned noodle. In the case of mundane or naturally ocurring toxins such as the venom of a coral snake or poison of a poison dart frog this effect is immediate and flawless. In the case of exotic poisons from outside the natural essence of Creation, such as Yozi venom or antifreeze tapped from the veins of Autochthon, the moonsilver can be more difficult to read. Simple contact with the toxins triggers the reaction, same as mundane poisons, but the utensils act as Exceptional Gear for a (Perception + Awareness) roll, difficulty 3. If successful, the user is able to read the subtle ripples in the moonsilver and is alerted to the presence of the poison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 01-19-2023, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T11:53:21-08:00","id":1500749,"title":"","content":"Must admit that the image of moonsilver tarnishing in contact with the poison got my mind thinking of taking things a step further - what if the utensils darkening were not only a sign of the detection of poison, but its absorption/cleansing by the chopsticks?<br /> <br /> Now i'm imagining developing a whole set of evocations out of extracting, storing and them wielding those same poisons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T13:00:00-08:00","id":1500763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1500737-chary-counselor-s-setting-artifact-\u25cf\u25cf?p=1500749#post1500749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Must admit that the image of moonsilver tarnishing in contact with the poison got my mind thinking of taking things a step further - what if the utensils darkening were not only a sign of the detection of poison, but its absorption/cleansing by the chopsticks?<br /> <br /> Now i'm imagining developing a whole set of evocations out of extracting, storing and them wielding those same poisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The silver tarnishing thing is a real(ish) thing. It's one of the reasons Korean chopsticks are metal and flat. Silver allegedly reacts to poison, so the wealthy had their utensils made of silver to thwart possible assassination attempts, Commoners had them made out of iron/steel so it could look like they were wealthy and had silver, and in both cases metal is expensive so the chopsticks became the small, flat ones we know today to cut costs on materials.<br /> <br /> Your evocation ideas sound amazeballs, though! Please keep me in the loop if you ever decide to take a crack at em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}